§ `s 6 -- does my child meet the immunisation requirements`

-- c003 (Chloe, 2003) and c065 (Oliver, 2030): vaccinated on the schedule. s 6 has no objection ground.
#ASSERT `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` `Chloe in 2003, vaccinated on the schedule`
#ASSERT `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` `Oliver, immunised on the schedule`
#ASSERT `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` `a child with a certified contraindication`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` `a child of a parent who objects to vaccination`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my child meet the immunisation requirements` `an unvaccinated child with no certificate`

§ `s 61B, Sch 1 cl 7(2) -- what failing them does to my FTB`

-- c065: met within the 63-day grace period, no reduction; missed it, the reduction runs from the notice date.
#ASSERT NOT `Will my FTB child rate be reduced` TRUE 63
#ASSERT `Will my FTB child rate be reduced` TRUE 64
#ASSERT `Will my FTB child rate be reduced` FALSE 100

#ASSERT `For how many days will my FTB child rate be reduced` TRUE 100 EQUALS 100

#ASSERT `What is my annual FTB child rate on a reduced day` `printed` FALSE EQUALS 3555.10
#ASSERT `What is my annual FTB child rate on a reduced day` `printed` TRUE EQUALS 4843.55

§ `s 22 -- is my child an FTB child; s 21 -- am I eligible`

-- k054: Ruby is an FTB child whether or not her parents are married.
#ASSERT `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `Ruby, born to unmarried parents`
#ASSERT `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `Ruby, after her parents marry`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `a 16 year old who has left school`
#ASSERT `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `a 19 year old still at school, in the year of turning 19`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my child an FTB child of mine` `a 19 year old at school after that year has ended`

#ASSERT `Am I eligible for family tax benefit` `Ruby, born to unmarried parents` TRUE 5000 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for family tax benefit` `Ruby, born to unmarried parents` TRUE 5000 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for family tax benefit` `Ruby, born to unmarried parents` TRUE 0 FALSE

§ `Sch 1 Parts 2 and 3 -- how much FTB Part A`

-- c064: Oliver's FTB Part A on a family income of $70,000 (ASSUMED): maximum 4292.40 + 600 = 4892.40; income tested
-- 4892.40 - 20% x 30000 = -1107.60; the base rate 1416.20 + 600 = 2016.20 is higher, so 2016.20.
-- $100,000: Method 2; no supplement (over $80,000); provisional 1416.20 - 30% x 1012 = 1112.60. $120,000: nil.
-- On a benefit, $50,000: no income reduction (cl 38L), 4892.40.
#ASSERT `Is my FTB Part A worked out by Method 1` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver, family income 70000`

#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver, family income 70000` EQUALS 2016.20
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `a couple with one child, family income 100000` EQUALS 1112.60
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `a couple with one child, family income 120000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `a parent on a benefit with one child, income 50000` EQUALS 4892.40
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `Graham and Sue with Chloe and Jake` EQUALS 9784.80
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part A do I get a year` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver and Ella` EQUALS 2832.40

§ `Sch 1 Part 4 -- how much FTB Part B`

-- Single, youngest 6: 1781.20 + 302.95 = 2084.15, no income test. Couple, lower earner $14,000, youngest 2: 2872.55 - 20% x
-- 10000 = 872.55. Higher earner over $100,000: nil. Couple, youngest 13: nil, unless grandparents (2084.15).
-- d040: on a day parental leave pay is payable to Daniel, Priya's Part B is nil (cl 28C).
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `a single parent of a 6 year old, income 50000` EQUALS 2084.15
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `a couple whose lower earner has 14000` EQUALS 872.55
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `a couple whose higher earner has 110000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `a couple whose youngest child is 13` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `grandparents caring for a 13 year old` EQUALS 2084.15
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `Priya and Daniel on a day of parental leave pay` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much FTB Part B do I get a year` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver and Ella` EQUALS 2872.55

-- k002: 9784.80 + 2872.55. c071: 2832.40 + 2872.55.
#ASSERT `How much family tax benefit do I get a year` `printed` `Graham and Sue with Chloe and Jake` EQUALS 12657.35
#ASSERT `How much family tax benefit do I get a year` `printed` `Chloe and Liam with Oliver and Ella` EQUALS 5704.95

§ `Sch 1 cl 35A, s 58AA -- the newborn supplement and the upfront payment`

-- c064, d040, k054. Parental leave pay for the child (or a partner's flexible PPL day) means no supplement, and so no $500.
#ASSERT `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `a married parent with no parental leave pay, day 5`
#ASSERT NOT `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `the same parent on day 91`
#ASSERT NOT `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `Chloe, paid parental leave pay for Oliver`
#ASSERT NOT `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `Priya, whose partner Daniel is paid for flexible PPL days`
#ASSERT `Is newborn supplement added for the day` `Tahlia, unmarried, with no parental leave pay`

#ASSERT `How much newborn upfront payment do I get` `printed` `Tahlia, unmarried, with no parental leave pay` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much newborn upfront payment do I get` `printed` `Chloe, paid parental leave pay for Oliver` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much newborn upfront payment do I get` `printed` `Priya, whose partner Daniel is paid for flexible PPL days` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much newborn upfront payment do I get` `printed` `a married parent with no parental leave pay, day 5` FALSE FALSE 50 EQUALS 250

§ `when the Act can answer`

-- d002 (1996) predates the Act (No. 80 of 1999). k002 (2006) and the 2030s events can be asked of it.
#ASSERT NOT `Could this Act apply to my event in that year` 1996
#ASSERT `Could this Act apply to my event in that year` 2006

§ `s 85BA -- the Child Care Subsidy for a session`

-- c066 and c065: unimmunised, Oliver's sessions attract no CCS at all.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for CCS for the session` `Oliver at long day care, immunised`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for CCS for the session` `Oliver at long day care, not immunised`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for CCS for the session` `a session in the compulsory school program`

§ `Sch 2 cll 3, 3A, 3B -- the applicable percentage`

-- Taper and formula percentages (the last arguments) are HYPOTHETICAL inputs: the formulas are not in the deposit.
#ASSERT `What is my basic CCS percentage` `printed` 70000 0 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `What is my basic CCS percentage` `printed` 200000 70 EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `What is my basic CCS percentage` `printed` 530000 0 EQUALS 0

-- c071: Ella, under 6, with Oliver (older, under 6) also in care, is a higher rate child; Oliver is not.
#ASSERT `Is my child a higher rate child` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my child a higher rate child` TRUE FALSE

-- c071 at $90,000: other rate band 2, lesser of 95 and 93 (hypothetical) = 93, above the basic 89; in home care: basic 89.
-- $200,000: band 3, 80. $350,000: band 5, 50, but basic 52 is higher (cl 3A(2)).
#ASSERT `What is my CCS percentage` `printed` 90000 `centre-based day care` TRUE 89 93 0 EQUALS 93
#ASSERT `What is my CCS percentage` `printed` 90000 `in home care` TRUE 89 93 0 EQUALS 89
#ASSERT `What is my CCS percentage` `printed` 200000 `centre-based day care` TRUE 75 0 0 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `What is my CCS percentage` `printed` 350000 `centre-based day care` TRUE 52 0 0 EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `What is my CCS percentage` `printed` 90000 `centre-based day care` FALSE 89 93 0 EQUALS 89

§ `Sch 2 cll 2, 11, 12, 1, 4 -- the hourly rate, subsidised hours and the fortnight`

#ASSERT `What is my hourly rate of CCS` `printed` `centre-based day care` 90 10 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `What is my hourly rate of CCS` `printed` `family day care` 90 15 EQUALS 9.99

-- The 3 day guarantee (72) and the increased hours result (100) for more than 48 hours; a couple takes the lower.
#ASSERT `How many hours are subsidised each fortnight` 0 0 FALSE EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `How many hours are subsidised each fortnight` 50 0 FALSE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `How many hours are subsidised each fortnight` 76 0 TRUE EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `How many hours are subsidised each fortnight` 48 60 TRUE EQUALS 72

-- c066: Oliver, three 10-hour days a week = 60 hours a fortnight (ASSUMED hours), at $9.00 an hour: all within the
-- guarantee, 540. Four 10-hour days (80 hours) on the guarantee: 72 subsidised, 648.
#ASSERT `How much CCS do I get for the fortnight` 9 60 72 EQUALS 540
#ASSERT `How much CCS do I get for the fortnight` 9 80 72 EQUALS 648

